#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""verify — drive scholia's CLI the way a user does, one feature at a time.

    verify/verify doctor              preflight: is this checkout ready to drive?
    verify/verify verify <feature>    drive one feature area (see verify/features/)
    verify/verify verify              the full sweep; exit 1 if any step fails
    verify/verify list                the feature areas, in sweep order

Each feature runs in its own tmux session on a private tmux socket, with its
own HOME, TMPDIR and data directory under one run directory, seeded from
demo/seed/. Nothing reads or writes your real vault or config: SCHOLIA_VAULT
is unset, HOME points at the run, and fastembed is blocked so no model is ever
downloaded. linkcheck is driven against a local HTTP stub on 127.0.0.1.

Every step is checked against the terminal floor invariants:
  INV-CRASH   no traceback on stderr
  INV-EXIT    a valid command exits 0; an invalid one exits non-zero and says why
  INV-HANG    every command finishes within --timeout seconds
  INV-SILENT  a command prints something (a lead, never a failure)
  INV-DURABLE persisted state reads back from a fresh session (explicit steps)
  INV-STRAY   nothing is written in the checkout or ~/.cache/scholia
plus the step's own expected output. Any breach but INV-SILENT fails the run.

Evidence (per-step stdout, stderr, exit code, the tmux transcript, and
summary.json) goes to --evidence DIR, default verify/.evidence/<UTC stamp>/;
teardown never deletes it. The last line printed is one machine-readable
summary: `VERIFY {"result": "pass"|"fail", ...}`.
"""
